credentialsd for Debian
=======================

Source tarball
--------------

The package builds without network access, from the Rust crates in vendor/.
Git does not contain them, so the .orig tarball is the one that `meson dist`
produces, which adds vendor/ and a .cargo/config that points Cargo at it
(build-aux/dist-vendor.sh). Releases up to 0.4.0 contain neither this
packaging nor the fix that lets `meson dist` vendor the crates, so build
from a git checkout that has both, and give the package a snapshot version:

    cd credentialsd
    meson setup _dist -Dfeature_demo_client=disabled
    meson dist -C _dist --no-tests --formats xztar
    VERSION=$(meson introspect --projectinfo _dist | jq -r .version)
    cd ..
    cp credentialsd/_dist/meson-dist/credentialsd-$VERSION.tar.xz \
       credentialsd_$VERSION.orig.tar.xz

Upstream keeps this packaging in distrib/debian/. Copy it to debian/ in
the unpacked tarball, set the version in debian/changelog (for example with
`dch -v $VERSION+git$(date +%Y%m%d)-1`, which also needs the .orig tarball
renamed to match), and build:

    tar xf credentialsd_$VERSION.orig.tar.xz
    cp -r credentialsd-$VERSION/distrib/debian credentialsd-$VERSION/debian
    cd credentialsd-$VERSION
    dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc

Vendored crates
---------------

Building against vendored crates is fine for third-party repositories such
as the openSUSE Build Service. The Debian archive
expects each crate to be packaged on its own (see the Debian Rust team
policy), so an upload to Debian has to replace vendor/ with Build-Depends
on librust-*-dev packages.
